# Nulls: arithmetic and comparisons with null are null, `and`/`or` use three-valued logic, and
# `where` keeps only true rows (LANGUAGE.md §4).
mode: run
---- query
from '../../data/edge/nulls.csv'
| project id, plus = value + 1, cmp = value > 2, both = value > 2 and isnotnull(name), either = value > 2 or id == 5
| sort by id asc
---- expected
id   | plus   | cmp   | both  | either
long | real   | bool  | bool  | bool
-----+--------+-------+-------+-------
   1 |    2.5 | false | false | false
   2 |    3.5 | true  | false | true
   3 | null   | null  | null  | null
   4 |    5.5 | true  | true  | true
   5 | null   | null  | false | true
